      "note": {
        "name": "Gatekeeper IIIb",
        "why_it_works": "The exit lane holds two trucks, B and D, and both can only leave by dropping into the bottom rows, which truck H and car J are sitting on. H can only slide left once car F clears column 2, and F can only get out by going up through the red car's row. That forces the counter-intuitive opening: move the red car backwards to make room.",
        "what_it_teaches": "Introduces trucks blocking the exit row, and the idea that the red car can be its own blocker. Players learn to read a dependency chain backwards from the exit (D needs the corner, the corner needs H, H needs F) instead of attacking the nearest obstacle."
      }
    },
