      "note": {
        "name": "Gatekeeper IVb",
        "why_it_works": "Builds on IIIb with car K standing in the lane next to exit truck D. K can only leave downwards, so B, D and K all have to drop through the same bottom-right gap that H and J vacate. The left-side shuffle (C, E, F and the red car backing up) also gets one step longer, because C now has to drop all the way to the bottom.",
        "what_it_teaches": "Ordering under pressure: clear the bottom rows once, then let three vehicles fall through in sequence. It's the harder follow-up to IIIb, so a player who has just learned that backing up the red car is allowed has to apply it again inside a longer chain."
      }
